*.test

# Fitting inputs and outputs (cmd/fit-physical, cmd/render-physical).
#
# reference/ holds recordings used as timbre-match targets. Most are not the
# repository's to redistribute and nothing in the test suite may depend on
# them — see docs/physical-measured-fit.md. The exception is the CC BY 4.0
# subset re-included at the bottom of this file, which is committed precisely
# so a fit can be reproduced from the repository alone; reference/CREDITS.md
# carries its licence and provenance. The pattern is reference/* rather than
# reference/ because git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# itself excluded.
#
# fits/ holds everything a run leaves in writing — its report, its checkpoint
# and its progress log — and renders/ holds the audio. Both are ignored
# wholesale, and the tools create them on demand, so a run's artifacts never
# land in the project root again. One set per run when several are compared
# side by side: fits/fit-hertzian.{json,checkpoint,log} beside
# renders/fit-hertzian.wav. The log is a shell redirect of stderr rather than
# anything the tool opens, so keeping it next to the report is a convention the
# justfile documents and nothing enforces. A report is derived from a recording
# the repository does not contain, so it cannot be committed as evidence
# anyway — quote its numbers in docs/ and commit the figures.
reference/*
fits/
renders/
# Belt and braces for a run pointed somewhere else by hand: a checkpoint is
# never a source file, whatever it ends up being called, no WAV in this
# repository is either, and a stray fit log in the root is still a fit log.
*.checkpoint
*.wav
fit-*.log
fit-summary.txt
fit-progress.txt

# The committed reference subset. These negations must come after *.wav above,
# because the last matching pattern wins. Only the medium-pitch head strikes are
# carried: they are the set the fit uses, and the full 336-file pack is 126 MB
# against 5.5 MB for these sixteen. Licence and provenance in reference/CREDITS.md.
!reference/CREDITS.md
!reference/tt08x08-mp-hd-v[0-9][0-9].wav

# Built by `go build ./cmd/fit-physical` and `./cmd/render-physical`
/fit-physical
/render-physical
